// A dip, then an ember pacing the pit where the stone lies; three generations of bloom fill the pit and quench it; a fenced ember, a dip and a climb beyond.
name Quench
rule B1234/S012345678
steps 3
hint An ember paces the pit where the stone lies. Drop in when it is far, plant, jump back out, and Grow: three generations of bloom fill the pit and put the ember out. Another ember walks the road beyond.
tip Growth takes whatever stands inside it, ember or wanderer. Stand back on the rock, clear of the pit's edge, before you grow. The bloom's top is two cells above the ground.
intro Something still burns down there. The old growth left embers behind, and embers hate what grows: a bloom puts them out. Plant beneath one and see.
outro The ember went out in the bloom. What grows again does not burn.
